%T A402191 18849563,56871545,171330471,516108020,1553484175,4675404086,
%U A402191 14065071878,42306586745,127220980609,382522332140,1149947615310,3456629446665,10388960564508
%N A402191 Number of distinct hyperplanes through the center of the (n-1)-dimensional permutohedron that are spanned by its ridges (faces of codimension 2).
%C A402191 The permutohedron of order n is the convex hull of the n! permutations of (1, 2, ..., n); it has dimension n-1. Its ridges correspond to the ordered set partitions of {1, ..., n} into three blocks, so there are A001117(n) of them. Each ridge together with the center spans a hyperplane; a(n) counts the distinct hyperplanes obtained.
%C A402191 A ridge whose blocks have sizes (a, b, c) with a != c spans a hyperplane shared only with the reversed partition; ridges with a = c give hyperplanes with a two-valued normal, counted by T(n) in the formula.
%D A402191 G. M. Ziegler, Lectures on Polytopes, Springer, Graduate Texts in Mathematics 152, 1995, Example 0.10.
%H A402191 DICTO, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24121177">DICTO 1:2 Truncated Octahedron: The 4D Vacuus of the Permutohedron</a>, Zenodo (2026), Theorem 3.
%F A402191 a(n) = Sum_{a,b,c >= 1, a+b+c = n, a < c} n!/(a!*b!*c!) + T(n), where T(n) = 2^(n-1) - 1 for n odd and T(n) = 2^(n-2) - 1 for n even.
%e A402191 a(3) = 3: the hexagon's 6 vertices lie on its 3 long diagonals.
%e A402191 a(4) = 15: the truncated octahedron has 36 edges; 3 planes through its center contain 4 edges each and 12 planes contain 2 edges each, and 3*4 + 12*2 = 36.
%o A402191 (Python)
%o A402191 from math import factorial as F
%o A402191 def a(n):
%o A402191     s = sum(F(n)//(F(i)*F(n-i-k)*F(k)) for i in range(1, n) for k in range(i+1, n) if n-i-k >= 1)
%o A402191     return s + (2**(n-1)-1 if n % 2 else 2**(n-2)-1)
%o A402191 print([a(n) for n in range(3, 29)])
%Y A402191 Cf. A001117 (number of ridges), A002426, A400949.
%K A402191 nonn,new
%O A402191 3,1
%A A402191 _James Baker_, Nov 14 2026
